---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
import { APP, PUBLISHER } from '../lib/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — HelloNotes"
  description="HelloNotes collects nothing: no account, no analytics, no tracking, no servers. Your notes are plain files on your own device."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  intro="Last updated: 2026"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-6 py-12">
    <Prose>
      <p>
        {APP.name} is a <strong>local-first</strong> application published by{' '}
        {PUBLISHER.legalName} Your notes are stored as plain files on your own device, in a folder
        you select.{' '}
        <strong>
          We do not collect, transmit, sell, or have access to your notes or any personal data.
        </strong>
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        <p>
          <strong>In short:</strong> no account, no analytics, no tracking, no servers. Your data
          never leaves your device unless you explicitly choose to sync it somewhere yourself.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. {APP.name} has no analytics, no telemetry, no advertising identifiers, and no user
        accounts. We do not operate any server that receives your data. Because we hold no data
        about you, there is nothing for us to disclose, share, or delete on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Your notes</h2>
      <p>
        Your notes are ordinary Markdown files in a folder on your device that you choose. They
        remain under your control and can be read or edited by any other application. {APP.name}{' '}
        reads and writes only the folders you explicitly open, using the OS's security-scoped file
        access.
      </p>

      <h2>On-device intelligence</h2>
      <p>
        The optional AI features — Summarise, Suggest Tags and Links, Rewrite, New Note from a
        Prompt, “Ask your library” and the Assistant — use Apple’s Foundation Models framework on
        your device: Apple Intelligence, or an open model you choose to download and run on your
        device with MLX. Your note content is processed locally and is <strong>not</strong> sent to
        us or to any third party. {APP.name} has no third-party AI services and stores no AI
        credentials; API keys stored by earlier versions are deleted from your device.
      </p>
      <p>
        Downloading an MLX model contacts Hugging Face to fetch the model’s files; none of your
        notes are sent. When you ask the Assistant to search or read the web, or run research for a
        new note, the search terms and addresses it uses go to that search engine or website.
      </p>

      <h2>Cloud storage and version control</h2>
      <p>
        If you keep a collection in iCloud Drive, Dropbox, Box, OneDrive or Google Drive, or connect
        one of those accounts directly, your files are handled by that service under its own privacy
        policy — the same as any other folder on your device. Similarly, if you use the built-in Git
        features with your own remote repository, your notes are sent only to the destination{' '}
        <em>you</em> configure. {APP.name} is not that destination and does not receive a copy.
      </p>

      <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>{APP.name} does not collect data from anyone, including children, and is rated 4+.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a revised date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.email}`}>{PUBLISHER.email}</a>,
        or see the <a href={href('/support')}>support page</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
